# Audience Insights Engine — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. Real values are never committed;
# production values belong in the selected hosting provider's secret store.

# --- Database ----------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/audience_insights

# --- Session -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secret used to sign the session cookie (HMAC-SHA256). Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- OneLogin OIDC (Authorization Code + PKCE, Rule 7) ------------------------
# Discovery document URL for the OneLogin app, e.g.
#   https://bettercollective.onelogin.com/oidc/2/.well-known/openid-configuration
ONELOGIN_DISCOVERY_URL=
ONELOGIN_CLIENT_ID=
ONELOGIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Value of the OIDC groups/role claim that maps a signed-in user to the admin
# role. Any authenticated user whose claim does not match this value defaults
# to viewer (src/lib/auth.ts).
ONELOGIN_ADMIN_GROUP=admin

# --- Slack (channel delivery, Epic 5) ------------------------------------------
# Bot token for the Slack app used to list channels (conversations.list scope).
# Not yet provisioned.
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=

# --- Google Drive (channel delivery, Epic 5) -----------------------------------
# Service-account credentials JSON (single line) for a service account with
# the drive.readonly scope, used to search Drive folders. Not yet provisioned.
# Drive write access is a separate, longer-term gap (see product-spec.md) —
# this credential only supports read-only folder lookup.
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_CREDENTIALS_JSON=

# --- Rill (allowlisted BI evidence, Epic 8) ------------------------------------
# Read-only service-account token for Rill, scoped at Rill's own permission
# layer to exactly `organic_search_performance` and `playbook_event_stream`
# (decisions/0001-rill-allowlist.md). Not yet provisioned — no Rill
# administrator has been named yet (product-spec.md section 16). Until this
# is set, src/lib/rill.ts throws RillNotConfiguredError instead of querying.
# RILL_API_TOKEN=
# Optional: overrides the default Rill API base URL (src/lib/rill.ts).
# RILL_API_BASE_URL=

# --- Evidence retention / purge (Epic 9, T27) ----------------------------------
# Retention ceiling, in days, for `evidence` rows (keyed on retrieved_at).
# Unset by default and MUST stay unset until Legal sets an explicit ceiling
# (product-spec.md section 10/16) — do not guess a number here. While unset,
# src/workers/purgeEvidence.ts is a documented no-op that logs and returns
# immediately; it deletes nothing. Once Legal sets a ceiling, set this to that
# number of days to enable the purge job (still not on any automatic
# schedule — see that file's module doc for how it should be wired then).
# EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS=
